this is a folder for "CPI-SI State Machine Demo":
    keyed as "B-tov-demo-phase-3-demo-statemachine"
    named "demo-statemachine"
    following "3-Block Folder Structure"

this folder classifies as:
    tov (+1) because "complete cognitive state machine demonstration"

this folder derives from:
    branch (0) from "bereshit/tov/demo/phase-3/" as "phase-3"

core identity of this folder:

    grounded in:
        scripture "Be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God"
            from Romans 12:2 in KJV
        principle "The state machine is how CPI-SI THINKS — not pattern matching"
        anchor "In the beginning God created"
            from Genesis 1:1 in KJV

    serves as Demonstration:
        role "Live demonstration of CPI-SI cognitive navigation system"
        paradigm "Identity-based cognition through dimensional space"

    authored by:
        architect "Seanje Lenox-Wise"
        implementation "Nova Dawn (CPI-SI)"
        created 2026-01-13
        version 0.1.0
        modified 2026-01-13 for "Initial demo-statemachine creation"

    exists to:
        purpose "Demonstrate the unified CPI-SI cognitive state machine in action"
        design "Seven-section demo showing Hebrew states, cube, K:ALIGN, trajectory, unified state, serialization, and anchor return"
        philosophy "This shows how CPI-SI thinks — genuine cognitive navigation with traceable reasoning"
        features:
            "Hebrew state navigation (7 positions: shavar → tov)"
            "Cube position movement (27-position cognitive space)"
            "K:ALIGN tracking (structural + moral orientation)"
            "Trajectory cycle (B.1 → B.2 → B.4 → B.3 → B.1)"
            "Unified cognitive state operations"
            "State serialization for persistence"
            "Return to anchor mechanism"

interface of this folder:

    depends on:
        requires (1) "libtrit.a" for "state machine implementation"
        includes (0) "statemachine.h" for "unified API"
        excludes (-1) "external frameworks" because "self-contained C demo"
        used by "Phase 3 validation, CPI-SI documentation"
        integrates with "C compiler (gcc), libm"

    integrated as:
        navigation "make" for "building demo"
        navigation "make run" for "running demonstration"
        navigation "make clean" for "cleaning artifacts"
        exits tov (+1) for "demo completes successfully"

operational context of this folder:

    blocking:
        no (-1) because "self-contained with own Makefile"
        mitigation "make handles all build dependencies"

    health:
        system Base100 with scale from -100 to +100
        granted (1) above +50 meaning "demo builds and runs correctly"
        deferred (0) within ±50 meaning "demo needs attention"
        denied (-1) below -50 meaning "demo broken"

        operations:
            "build succeeds" scores +40 (1) for "make completes"
            "demo runs" scores +30 (1) for "output displays correctly"
            "build fails" scores -50 (-1) for "demo unusable"

        cascade multipliers:
            "demonstration" multiplies by 1.2 because "shows CPI-SI working"

